WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.741 --> 00:00:16.562
led the monks to his companions.

2
00:00:17.603 --> 00:00:20.825
The monks told the Tang Monk everything that they had told Wukong.

3
00:00:22.406 --> 00:00:24.007
terrible," said the Tang Monk.

4
00:00:24.588 --> 00:00:25.468
"We must help you."

5
00:00:26.469 --> 00:00:27.770
"Yes," the monkey agreed.

6
00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:30.772
"I'll deal with the Tiger Immortal in the morning."

7
00:00:31.872 --> 00:00:34.513
The monks knew of an empty building nearby.

8
00:00:36.433 --> 00:00:40.074
They led the travelers there, and everyone went to sleep for the night.

9
00:00:41.795 --> 00:00:43.876
The next morning Wukong woke up early.

10
00:00:45.796 --> 00:00:47.897
Someone was pounding on the door of the building.

11
00:00:48.937 --> 00:00:51.918
A voice boomed, "I am the Tiger Immortal!"

12
00:00:52.958 --> 00:00:54.779
The Tang Monk's eyes popped open.

13
00:00:56.719 --> 00:00:59.120
He and all the other monks trembled with fear.

14
00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:02.241
Wujing and Bajie drew their weapons.

15
00:01:03.582 --> 00:01:06.504
smiled. "Don't worry, everyone.

16
00:01:07.204 --> 00:01:08.305
I'll deal with this villain."

17
00:01:10.366 --> 00:01:11.666
The monkey went outside.

18
00:01:15.769 --> 00:01:16.169
are you?"

19
00:01:16.489 --> 00:01:17.950
demanded the Tiger Immortal.

20
00:01:17.970 --> 00:01:21.552
"I am Sun Wukong," said the monkey.

21
00:01:21.572 --> 00:01:24.033
"And you should be ashamed of yourself!

22
00:01:25.014 --> 00:01:29.196
Just because you're a little powerful, you think you can treat the Buddhist monks badly."

23
00:01:30.716 --> 00:01:32.017
"A little powerful?"

24
00:01:32.277 --> 00:01:34.138
The Tiger Immortal looked offended.

25
00:01:34.158 --> 00:01:37.000
"I am powerful!"

26
00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:39.321
Wukong laughed.

27
00:01:39.341 --> 00:01:42.102
"You're not as powerful as I am.

28
00:01:42.903 --> 00:01:45.504
Did you know that the Jade Emperor is afraid of me?

29
00:01:45.524 --> 00:01:48.866
I once defeated his entire army."

30
00:01:49.907 --> 00:01:52.188
The Tiger Immortal puffed out his chest.

31
00:01:53.508 --> 00:01:55.550
can summon rain," he said.

32
00:01:55.570 --> 00:01:57.691
"I doubt you can do that."

33
00:01:58.651 --> 00:01:59.572
Wukong snorted.

34
00:02:00.564 --> 00:02:01.665
"I can summon rain.

35
00:02:01.885 --> 00:02:02.426
It's easy."

36
00:02:02.446 --> 00:02:07.410
"Well then, let's have a contest," said the Tiger Immortal.

37
00:02:07.430 --> 00:02:10.672
"Whoever summons more rain is the winner.

38
00:02:11.553 --> 00:02:14.896
If you win, I'll let you and all the monks go free.

39
00:02:15.736 --> 00:02:20.120
But if I win, you must stay here and be my slaves."

40
00:02:21.641 --> 00:02:23.262
a fool," said Wukong.

41
00:02:23.282 --> 00:02:25.104
"I accept your challenge."

42
00:02:27.646 --> 00:02:30.008
The Tiger Immortal led everyone into town.

43
00:02:31.732 --> 00:02:34.253
In the center of town was a Daoist altar.

44
00:02:35.333 --> 00:02:40.295
A stone tablet, incense sticks, and papers with magic writing were on the altar.

45
00:02:41.075 --> 00:02:43.756
A crowd of people arrived to see what was going on.

46
00:02:43.776 --> 00:02:48.477
"I will go first," announced the Tiger Immortal.

47
00:02:49.357 --> 00:02:50.578
He walked toward the altar.

48
00:02:52.098 --> 00:02:53.338
Tang Monk shook his head.

49
00:02:53.358 --> 00:02:56.099
"This is terrible," he muttered.

50
00:02:56.919 --> 00:02:58.420
Bajie glanced at him.

51
00:02:59.588 --> 00:03:00.269
worry, Master.

52
00:03:00.609 --> 00:03:02.150
Wukong will win this contest."

53
00:03:02.230 --> 00:03:04.531
"But what if he doesn't win?"

54
00:03:04.851 --> 00:03:05.492
asked the monk.

55
00:03:06.572 --> 00:03:10.114
"We'll all be stuck here, forced to work for the Tiger Immortal.

56
00:03:11.275 --> 00:03:14.317
If that happens, we'll never reach the Western Paradise.

57
00:03:15.117 --> 00:03:17.919
The True Scriptures will never get to the Tang Empire."

58
00:03:18.799 --> 00:03:21.041
The monk buried his face in his hands.

59
00:03:22.541 --> 00:03:24.383
is right, Master," said Wujing.

60
00:03:24.403 --> 00:03:28.000
"We have nothing to worry about."

61
00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:29.942
Wukong stood by them, smiling.

62
00:03:30.762 --> 00:03:36.966
From the altar the Tiger Immortal called out, "I will now pray to Heaven for rain!"

63
00:03:40.149 --> 00:03:44.131
The Tiger Immortal lit the incense and then sat down.

64
00:03:45.172 --> 00:03:47.994
He closed his eyes and began to recite a spell.

65
00:03:50.035 --> 00:03:52.137
Next he lit one of the papers on fire.

66
00:03:54.138 --> 00:03:56.520
When that one went out, he lit another paper.

67
00:03:59.792 --> 00:04:01.713
Soon all of the papers were gone.

68
00:04:03.793 --> 00:04:07.554
The Tiger Immortal lifted the stone tablet and then slammed it down.

69
00:04:10.355 --> 00:04:11.975
There was a gasp from the crowd.

70
00:04:12.856 --> 00:04:15.916
Wukong looked up at the sky, which was becoming dark.

71
00:04:17.197 --> 00:04:19.957
Wind blew and dark clouds moved in.

72
00:04:20.638 --> 00:04:21.678
Thunder rumbled.

73
00:04:22.918 --> 00:04:23.978
Tang Monk trembled.

74
00:04:23.998 --> 00:04:24.859
"Oh no!

75
00:04:25.339 --> 00:04:25.939
It's working!

76
00:04:26.419 --> 00:04:27.239
It's going to rain!"

77
00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:30.693
chuckled. "You all wait here.

78
00:04:31.213 --> 00:04:32.094
I'll be right back."

79
00:04:32.834 --> 00:04:35.936
The monkey recited a quick spell and then left his body.

80
00:04:39.899 --> 00:04:44.201
Up in the sky, he found the Old Woman of the Wind fanning the clouds.

81
00:04:45.422 --> 00:04:48.044
The Dragon King of the Eastern Sea was approaching.

82
00:04:49.905 --> 00:04:51.766
called out, "Stop what you're doing!

83
00:04:52.747 --> 00:04:53.507
Don't make any
